Ladybird resolves a Date’s local wall time in milliseconds and
uses the offset before a transition for both gaps and
overlaps. V8’s ICUTimezoneCache::GetOffsets(), JavaScriptCore’s
DateCache::calculateLocalTimeOffset(), and SpiderMonkey’s
TimeZone::GetUTCOffsetMs() use the former offset for both cases.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 agreed on the
skipped and repeated hours in Sydney and New York in 2024 and 2500. In
Sydney the local times immediately before and after each transition also
agreed. The crash report did not include its local time or zone.
